                        kind @errata
                        text "This node was completed on 2026-07-30 with no decision entry, only Todo to Doing to Done, and it did not deliver what its own description called the endgame. Verified against the source on 2026-07-31. Of the three steps described: Node.shellpath is Option<BString> at src/graph.rs:44, so the eager copy in the no-quote case is gone — shipped. The duplicate map key is gone, NodeIndex holding Vec<Option<NodeId>> at src/graph/index.rs:30 and comparing probe bytes against nodes[id].path — shipped. The endgame, a single append-only byte arena for all path text with nodes holding u32 offset and length spans, did not ship: Node.path at src/graph.rs:42 is still a BString, an individually heap-allocated buffer per node. Two of three, with the third silently dropped. The gap matters now rather than as bookkeeping, because ronin-node-locality-at-scale has measured per-edge cost rising 62% between 4,000 and 200,000 statements against C samurai's 26%, and four hundred thousand separate path allocations walked in traversal order is the leading hypothesis for that shape. The remaining work is not re-opened here: it belongs to that node, which already carries the instruction to confirm what shipped before proposing arena work and to judge it against measured cache-miss rates rather than against the assumption. Blast radius for whoever takes it: 82 non-test uses of .path. The process failure is worth naming separately from the technical one — a node whose description sets out an endgame should not reach Done without a decision entry saying whether that endgame was delivered, deferred or abandoned, and this one reached it with no entry at all, which is why the discrepancy survived a day and was found only by reading the source for an unrelated reason."
                        after_done true
