                    {
                        id kati-observation-session
                        title "Move command results, used-variable tracking, and statistics into the session"
                        deps (kati-session-value)
                        sealed true
                        log (
                            {
                                at 2026-08-04T18:10:00.331184339Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Scope for this node, made explicit because the parent inventory left one of these unowned.\n\nFour statics: COMMAND_RESULTS in func.rs, ALL_STATS in stats.rs together with the per-call-site STATS that each invocation of the two statistics macros expands to, USED_UNDEFINED_VARS in eval.rs, and USED_ENV_VARS in var.rs. SHELL_STATUS in var.rs belongs here too and had no owner before: it is the value behind .SHELLSTATUS, written by the shell builtin and read by the variable the scope binds, so it is per-evaluation state and not a cache.\n\nThe two used-variable sets are read from get_global_var and lookup_var_global, so they are entangled with the variable scope rather than independent of it, and they will likely have to move in the same change as kati-session-value rather than after it. If that turns out to be true, say so and move them there instead of threading a second session-shaped parameter into the same call sites twice.\n\nThe statistics macros are the awkward part, because each expansion creates its own static and the count therefore grows with call sites rather than being a fixed list. Whatever replaces them has to be reachable from a macro body with only the session in scope."
                            }

                            {
