                                text "Verified the isolation end to end twice. An --update run and a second comparison-only run each created a distinct detached GNU Make 4.4.1 worktree, classified exactly 1,349 cases as 606 unclassified / 74 compiler / 110 interface / 559 narration, exited zero, and left neither a target/make-upstream.* directory nor a registered auxiliary worktree. The clean inventory differs from the formerly polluted baseline by 28 removed and 28 added rows. cargo test --workspace --all-targets, the 12 focused classifier tests, sh -n, git diff --check, nplan lint, and spec validation pass. The repository's broader Clippy baseline is independently red under Clippy 1.97 on untouched code (the release command also applies pedantic lints to the Kati path dependency); no lint findings point at this shell/inventory change."
