                priority 0
                kind @test
                children (
                    {
                        id make-corpus-features
                        title "Port Make language-feature intent into owned graph and effect cases"
                        priority 1
                        kind @test
                        deps (make-build-intent-gate)
                        sealed true
                        log (
                            {
                                at 2026-08-08T12:12:13.65782247Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "One of three lanes growing `tests/make/` from GNU Make's own scenarios. This one takes `reference/gnumake/tests/scripts/features/`.\n\nThe point is coverage of behaviour we already claim, not finding new defects — though it will find some. Every case is a makefile written here from behaviour probed off /usr/bin/make 4.4.1, never copied: upstream's scripts are GPLv3 and `reference/gnumake` is a pinned checkout for exactly that reason (`make-licence-position`).\n\nCase names take a `feature-` prefix so three lanes writing concurrently cannot collide.\n\nA case that means to test a value writes it to a file — the harness compares exit status and file effect, never output. That excludes any scenario whose whole content is a diagnostic; skip those and say which, rather than contorting a case around it.\n\nWhere a case fails, record a `divergence` file naming the defect and, if one exists, the node. Do not fix code — that is another lane's ground this wave, and a divergence file that turns out to be already-fixed is caught automatically, because the suite fails when a recorded divergence starts passing."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-09T12:58:39.585481114Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-09T13:03:16.949335122Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @decision
                                text "Ported 60 repository-owned Make language-feature cases, taking the build-intent corpus from 51 to 111 cases. Each expected effect was recorded from /usr/bin/make GNU Make 4.4.1; the cases compare normal success/failure and filesystem effects, never GNU Make runner narration. Thirty-seven cases already compile to matching Ninja work. Twenty-three expose compiler gaps and carry bidirectional divergence markers: existing owners are make-vpath-search, make-include-semantics, make-option-carrying, make-assignment-modifiers, and make-export-to-recipes; fourteen newly concrete gaps have no dedicated WBS leaf yet. Output-only diagnostic scenarios remain discovery input under make-upstream-suite and are deliberately absent from this build-intent gate. The complete 111-case release run passes: an unrecorded divergence fails, and a fixed recorded divergence also fails until its marker is removed."
