                                kind @note
                                text "One of three lanes growing `tests/make/` from GNU Make's own scenarios. This one takes `reference/gnumake/tests/scripts/targets/` and `misc/`.\n\nThe point is coverage of behaviour we already claim, not finding new defects — though it will find some. Every case is a makefile written here from behaviour probed off /usr/bin/make 4.4.1, never copied: upstream's scripts are GPLv3 and `reference/gnumake` is a pinned checkout for exactly that reason (`make-licence-position`).\n\nCase names take a `target-` prefix so three lanes writing concurrently cannot collide.\n\nThis is the best-suited of the three sets, because a special target's whole effect is on what gets built and what is left behind — which is exactly what the harness compares. `tests/make/intermediate-is-removed` and `tests/make/secondary-is-kept` are the shape.\n\nWatch for the ones already covered: `.PHONY`, `.DEFAULT`, `.INTERMEDIATE`, `.SECONDARY`, `.NOTINTERMEDIATE`, `.IGNORE`, `.NOTPARALLEL`, `.SUFFIXES`, `.EXPORT_ALL_VARIABLES` and `.WAIT` all have cases already. Extend rather than duplicate, and prefer the combinations — a special target's interaction with another is where the gaps are.\n\nWhere a case fails, record a `divergence` file naming the defect and, if one exists, the node. Do not fix code — that is another lane's ground this wave."
