                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Measured on make-makeflags-residue-classification, 2026-08-09, against GNU Make 4.4.1 (/usr/bin/make). Found by naming the MAKEFLAGS share of the upstream residue; not fixed there because that node's subject was the classifier.\n\nA makefile that assigns MAKEFLAGS is writing to a switch table, not to a string. GNU Make re-reads the variable after each makefile and decodes the value back through decode_env_switches, then re-renders MAKEFLAGS from the table (define_makeflags, main.c). Ronin stores the literal text, acts on none of it, and renders nothing.\n\nTHREE CONSEQUENCES, each reproduced on its own.\n\n1. The switches never take effect. This is the build-outcome one.\n\n     MAKEFLAGS=-k\n     all: one two\n     one:; @false\n     two:; @echo TWO-RAN\n\n   GNU Make:  `make: *** [d1.mk:3: one] Error 1` / `TWO-RAN` /\n              `make: Target 'all' not remade because of errors.`   rc=2\n   Ronin:     `FAILED: [code=1] one` / `ronin: build stopped: subcommand failed.`   rc=2\n\n   Same status, different work: `two` is never built. -k asked for it. Reproduce this one through the build-intent gate — it is selected work, not narration.\n\n2. A plain assignment discards what the environment and the command line put there. Makefile `MAKEFLAGS=-w`, value read with `$(info $(MAKEFLAGS))`:\n\n     nothing else                GNU `w`                    Ronin `-w`\n     env MAKEFLAGS=-S            GNU `Sw`                   Ronin `-w`\n     command line `hello=world`  GNU `w -- hello=world`     Ronin `-w`\n\n   The `-- hello=world` half is MAKEOVERRIDES, which is how a command-line variable reaches a deeper unit, so this one is graph-affecting and not only spelling.\n\n3. `+=` appends text rather than adding a switch, so nothing is re-rendered and contradicting switches from different origins are never resolved. Makefile `MAKEFLAGS+=--no-print-directory` then `MAKEFLAGS+=-k`, command line `FOO=bar -r -R hello:=world`:\n\n     GNU    `rR --no-print-directory -- hello:=world FOO=bar`\n            then `krR --no-print-directory -- hello:=world FOO=bar`\n     Ronin  `rR -- hello:=world FOO=bar --no-print-directory`\n            then the same with ` -k` on the end\n\n   And with env `MAKEFLAGS=-w` against makefile `MAKEFLAGS+=--no-print-directory`: GNU renders `w`, because the environment beats the makefile (sv 63537); Ronin renders `w --no-print-directory` and so says two opposite things at once.\n\nWHERE IT LANDS\n`record_invocation_variables` in src/make/cli.rs removes the inherited MAKEFLAGS binding so kati can install its own file-origin recursive one, and nothing then reads back what the makefile assigns to it. `make-switch-precedence`'s closing note already carved out the neighbouring question — \"$(MAKEFLAGS) read inside a sub-make's own makefile still reports the parent's raw value, not the merge\" — and names the same two mechanisms (record_invocation's guard, and kati's read_invocation_state importing the process environment during evaluate). This is the other half of it: not what a parent hands down, but what the makefile itself writes.\n\nUPSTREAM SUITE\n28 of the 65 cases still unclassified in variables/MAKEFLAGS after the classifier fix are the -k/-S matrix at tests/scripts/variables/MAKEFLAGS:605-719, which is (1). The suite also asserts (2) and (3) throughout MAKEFLAGS:290-338 and :445-529; those land in makeflags-content, which is an interface observation and not by itself a defect claim."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-11T10:11:01.11937585Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "sealed — decomposition asserted complete (nplan seal)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-11T13:46:39.022589049Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "The Linux headers compatibility loop makes this concrete. At 36860b7, Kbuild's root `MAKEFLAGS += -rR` reaches the semantic self-child as a goal named `-rR` rather than as the no-builtins switches. Its `MAKECMDGOALS` becomes `-rR headers`, Kbuild consequently enables `need-config`, and compilation invents regeneration roots for absent `include/config/auto.conf{,.cmd}`; planning then dies before any recipe. Trace and control isolate the mechanism: GNU Make delegating `scripts/Makefile.build` directly to the same Ronin binary completes `headers`, while Ronin composing the self-child fails. Fix Makefile-assigned MAKEFLAGS decoding and prove both the focused child state and the real `/data/cap9p/linux` target."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-11T13:46:39.09463582Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-11T14:15:28.035547705Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Delivered GNU Make's special MAKEFLAGS assignment semantics at the evaluator boundary without adding an option parser to Kati. Each effective global write is decoded through Ronin's existing option grammar into a persistent switch table, protected environment/argv switches are reapplied last, MAKEFLAGS and MFLAGS are immediately canonicalized, MAKEOVERRIDES retains its recursive suffix, the normalized state reaches semantic children, and current-build scheduler controls such as -k are updated. Focused unit and process regressions pass; cargo test --workspace --all-targets passes; strict all-feature Clippy passes; direct/manifest equivalence covers 297 Makefiles and 276 graphs with zero disagreements. The real /data/cap9p/linux headers build no longer creates an -rR goal or auto.conf regeneration roots: it compiles 1,034 edges and reaches recipes, exposing the next existing make-newer-prerequisite-automatic-variable gap at KATI_NEW_INPUTS/find FORCE."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-11T14:15:28.251770985Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-11T14:21:42.001193475Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Post-completion GNU Make 4.4.1 inventory refresh confirms the broad effect: 62 recorded differences disappeared, from 1,368 to 1,306. The bounded classes are now 522 unclassified, 68 compiler candidates, 103 interface observations, and 613 narration observations (previously 522/69/168/609). Most removed rows were MAKEFLAGS content mismatches; one prior no-rule candidate now advances to an ordinary build-result difference. The versioned inventory was updated and its completeness gate passes."
                                after_done true
