            {
                id make-inherited-export-reassignment
                title "Preserve inherited export status across reassignment"
                kind @fix
                deps (make-export-to-recipes make-subninja-recursion)
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-08-11T12:38:43.528104432Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Own the BUGS.md three-level reproducer and Linux's exported `srcroot` reassignment. Importing an environment binding gives it GNU Make's default export attribute; a later accepted file-origin assignment changes its value without clearing that attribute. Semantic children and recipe environments must therefore receive the replacement value, while explicit `unexport` must still suppress it. This does not absorb the separate bare-export, target-specific-export, or evaluation-time-shell gaps owned by make-export-scope-semantics."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-11T12:38:47.572800836Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "sealed — decomposition asserted complete (nplan seal)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-11T12:38:53.379650275Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-11T12:52:20.301172525Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Preserve the inherited export attribute as a compiled environment delta, not by adding every imported name to Kati's explicit export map. An untouched environment value must cross recipes and semantic children as its original bytes — for example `RAW=$(EXPANDED)` stays literal even though `$(RAW)` inside the Makefile expands — while GNU Make deliberately keeps an inherited SHELL value in the process environment unless an export directive names SHELL. At the end of each unit, compare imported names with current global bindings: environment-origin bindings need no delta, a replacement binding exports its evaluated current value, and a removed binding emits an unset. Explicit export/unexport entries take precedence. Apply that same delta to the unit's recipes and descendant compiler environment."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-11T12:52:30.787692925Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "The BUGS.md regression failed before the change because two.mk sought inherited-before-child/included.mk; it now includes ./included.mk and records ROOT=. VALUE=inherited. The same test proves untouched `RAW=$(EXPANDED)` remains byte-literal and inherited SHELL remains /caller/shell. Green evidence: 74 CLI tests, the 304-case owned Make build-intent oracle, eight grouped-Make tests, 483 library tests (482 pass, one deliberately ignored), strict workspace/all-target/all-feature Clippy, the 297-Makefile direct/manifest equivalence gate with 276 graphs and zero disagreements, nplan check, lint, comments, audit, and diff checks. The pinned GNU Make 4.4.1 discovery inventory remains 1,368 rows and 69 compiler candidates; 12 rows change shape, with four unclassified and three interface observations becoming narration-only, producing 522 unclassified / 69 compiler / 168 interface / 609 narration. The real-project gate remains independently red after the earlier namespace correction, now at its next existing recursive-CMake gap: build_log.cc.o is missing with no known rule."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-11T12:53:31.570124178Z
