                text "Selected the first quiet-host Release-reference sweep as the new baseline. The pinned Ninja checkout remained at b51a1e37c2fb89bbefa600bd155e1ce13983f09d and was rebuilt with CMake Release flags (-O3 -DNDEBUG, -flto=auto), shrinking the stale 1,464,216-byte unoptimised binary to 430,528 bytes. Live preflight intervals showed 99% CPU idle, no blocked tasks, and no material I/O wait. The primary run used clean Ronin revision 3e6b9479835c5b55514b0de70aebc0c8a4f97a4d with two warmups and 15 interleaved samples; an immediate equal-size confirmation kept every tool median within 7.1% and each Ronin/Ninja ratio within 8.6%. Ronin is faster than Release Ninja and C samurai on seven of eight workloads; scheduler-barrier is 1.016x Ninja and 1.079x C, while every Ronin/Ninja peak-RSS ratio is below 1. baseline-v1.csv now exactly matches the primary raw output, with gate thresholds unchanged. Evidence: benchmarks/performance-validation-2026-08-10.{md,csv}; the 1-warmup/7-sample release gate passed, the baseline validation unit test passed, and the forced workspace check passed. The first forced workspace test run had one transient manifest-reload failure; that exact test passed three isolated reruns and the full forced suite passed on repetition."
