    {
        id ronin-response-file-write-diagnostic
        title "Say what Ninja says when a response file cannot be written"
        kind @fix
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-08-09T18:16:29.695734373Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Measured on ronin-exit-status-parity, 2026-08-09, against pinned Ninja b51a1e3. Not fixed there because the exit status already agrees and the node's subject was the status.\n\nManifest: a rule binding `rspfile = nodir/deeper/x.rsp` with `rspfile_content`, where `nodir` does not exist. Ninja does not create directories for a response file (build.cc StartEdge MakeDirs the outputs and the depfile, then WriteFile the rspfile), so the write fails before the command runs.\n\n  ninja  rc=1  stderr: ninja: error: WriteFile(nodir/deeper/x.rsp): Unable to create file. No such file or directory\n                stdout: ninja: build stopped: .\n  ronin  rc=1  stdout: ronin: build stopped: No such file or directory.\n\nThree differences, none of them the status. The operation and its path are not named, so the message does not say which file could not be written. The diagnostic is on stdout rather than stderr. And Ninja's `build stopped:` line carries an empty reason where Ronin folds the errno text into it — Ninja's reason string is empty here because the failure happened before any command produced one, which is itself worth reproducing rather than improving on.\n\nA conformance BuildCase for this shape cannot be added until the bytes agree; the status is already covered by the unit test ninja_build_makes_the_depfile_directory_and_not_the_response_file_directory. Add the case when this is fixed."
            }

            {
                at 2026-08-09T20:06:03.010124766Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Probed against pinned Ninja b51a1e3 on 2026-08-09; every shape below is measured, not remembered.\n\nNinja's `WriteFile` (src/disk_interface.cc:284) is stdio and reports itself through `Error()` on stderr, naming the call, the path and which of `fopen`/`fwrite`/`fclose` refused:\n\n  ninja: error: WriteFile(nodir/deeper/x.rsp): Unable to create file. No such file or directory\n  ninja: error: WriteFile(ro/x.rsp): Unable to create file. Permission denied\n  ninja: error: WriteFile(nested): Unable to create file. Is a directory\n  ninja: error: WriteFile(/dev/full): Unable to close the file. No space left on device      (payload < st_blksize)\n  ninja: error: WriteFile(/dev/full): Unable to write to the file. No space left on device    (payload >= st_blksize)\n\nThe step split is the stream buffer, which glibc sizes from the file's st_blksize: measured on /dev/full (blksize 4096) the boundary is exact — 4095 bytes is reported against the close, 4096 against the write. Ronin now writes through a BufWriter sized the same way, so the same failure earns the same sentence rather than a guessed one.\n\nBecause `WriteFile` never writes to the build loop's error string, Ninja's summary carries an empty reason: stdout gets `ninja: build stopped: .` and nothing else. Ronin said `ronin: build stopped: No such file or directory.` on stdout with an empty stderr — the file unnamed, the operation unnamed, the errno folded into the reason, and the whole thing on the wrong stream. Exit status agreed (1) before and after; that was never the defect.\n\nTwo further divergences fell out of the same `StartEdge` contract and are fixed here because the message fix alone would have left them wrong:\n\n- `-k 0` did not stop. Ninja returns ExitFailure the moment `StartEdge` fails, without consulting the allowance (build.cc:743); Ronin counted one failure and carried on. Measured with one bad edge ahead of two good ones under `-k 0 -j1`: Ninja built neither of the others, Ronin built both.\n- A failed manifest regeneration must not stop the run. `RebuildManifest` returns false with `err` still empty, and ninja.cc:1900 asks `!err.empty()` before reporting — so an empty reason is indistinguishable from a regeneration that had nothing to do, and Ninja goes on to build the requested targets and exits 0. Ronin turned it into `ronin: error: rebuilding 'build.ninja': ...` and exited 1. `BuildStop::already_reported` now keys off the same emptiness.\n\nAlso corrected while here: the response file's removal is armed only once the write succeeded. Ninja removes it in `FinishCommand`, after the command has run, so a write that failed never reaches the removal — Ronin was arming it before the write and would have tried to unlink a path it never created, `/dev/full` included.\n\nFive conformance BuildCases added (build outcome: 65 → 70 cases), each matched byte for byte on both streams and on status 1: missing directory, rspfile that is a directory, keep-going past an unwritable rspfile, and the two /dev/full payload sizes. The permission-denied shape is covered by hand-probe only — the BuildCase harness writes files, not modes, so it cannot build a read-only directory; its bytes are recorded above and are the same sentence as the missing-directory case.\n\nRemaining known divergence, NOT introduced here and out of this node's scope: after any manifest regeneration, Ninja's progress total carries the regeneration edge into the following build's denominator — a plain successful regeneration then two commands prints `[1/3] [2/3]` where Ronin prints `[1/2] [2/2]`. StatusPrinter's total_edges_ is moved by EdgeAddedToPlan/EdgeRemovedFromPlan and BuildStarted() resets only started/finished/running (status_printer.cc:89, 286). Filed as ronin-regeneration-progress-total.\n\nVerified: sandboxed `cargo test --workspace` green, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean, `cargo fmt --check -p ronin` clean (the two remaining workspace fmt diffs are in the pinned kati submodule at cf6b064 and predate this change), `scripts/check-ninja-conformance.sh` green with all 425 upstream tests passing."
            }

            {
                at 2026-08-09T20:10:03.136477509Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
            }

            {
                at 2026-08-10T18:08:28.453135559Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @errata
                text "Recovery audit on 2026-08-10: the prior Doing → Done log and delivery commit 11900e8 are valid, and 11900e8 is already an ancestor of current main, but the node's completion assertion did not survive later plan integration, so nplan exposed the node as Todo again. Every delivery path — src/build.rs, src/build/command.rs, src/build/tests.rs, src/cli.rs, src/error.rs, src/os.rs, and examples/conformance.rs — is unchanged since 11900e8. Current-source verification passed the focused response-file creation/diagnostic test, failed-command cleanup test, and /dev/full buffer-boundary invariant; the immediately preceding full differential run on the same source passed all 425 pinned Ninja tests, 10 CLI/tool comparisons, 86 build-outcome cases (including all five response-file cases), 3 invocation cases, persistence, and log-content checks; and the forced nplan workspace check is green. No implementation correction is needed. Restoring the manual completion assertion records shipped reality; this recovery requires no violation bypasses."
            }

            {
