                at 2026-08-09T20:03:17.993256054Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "`cargo fmt --all -- --check` — the commit gate's format check and scripts/check-release.sh line 13 — has been failing since kati was pinned at cf6b064 (this repo's 133fe3e, \"Pin the kati that compiles\"). The whole of it is import ordering in kati/src-rs/evaluate.rs: cf6b064's semantic-merge resolution added `use crate::{error_loc, log};` at line 39, where rustfmt wants it after `use crate::var::...` at line 46. Nothing else in the tree is unformatted; `cargo fmt --check -p ronin` is clean.\n\nConfirmed pre-existing by stashing ronin-indent-error-location's changes and re-running the check on the untouched branch: same single diff, same two hunks.\n\nNot fixed there because it is not that node's code and the remedy is not local to this repo. Fixing it means a commit *in the submodule* — which 133fe3e did with git plumbing, since kati is not nplan-governed and this repo's commit guard only knows this repo — and then bumping the submodule pointer, which moves a pin the conformance-corpus ship placed deliberately. That is a decision about the pin, not about formatting, so it wants its own commit and a Make-gate run behind it rather than a drive-by inside an unrelated change.\n\nUntil then every rust-touching commit has to bypass with `format-failed`, which is the cost of leaving it. ronin-indent-error-location is the first to do so."
            }

