    {
        id ronin-regeneration-progress-total
        title "Carry a regeneration edge into the progress total the way Ninja does"
        kind @fix
        log (
            {
                at 2026-08-09T20:09:58.21138517Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Measured on ronin-response-file-write-diagnostic, 2026-08-09, against pinned Ninja b51a1e3. Found while probing what a failed manifest regeneration does after it stops reporting itself as an error; it is not caused by that fix and reproduces on a plainly successful regeneration.\n\nManifest — a generator edge for build.ninja and two ordinary commands, with build.ninja backdated so the regeneration has something to do:\n\n  rule regen\n    command = touch $out\n    generator = 1\n  rule cp\n    command = cp $in $out\n  build build.ninja: regen conf\n  build a: cp source\n  build b: cp source\n  default a b\n\n  ninja -j1  rc=0  stdout: [1/1] touch build.ninja / [1/3] cp source a / [2/3] cp source b\n  ronin -j1  rc=0  stdout: [1/1] touch build.ninja / [1/2] cp source a / [2/2] cp source b\n\nNinja's denominator is three where Ronin's is two. `StatusPrinter::total_edges_` is moved only by `EdgeAddedToPlan` and `EdgeRemovedFromPlan` (status_printer.cc:89, 103), and `BuildStarted()` resets `started_edges_`, `finished_edges_` and `running_edges_` but deliberately not the total (status_printer.cc:286). One `Status` object serves both the manifest-regeneration builder and the build that follows, so the regeneration edge stays in the total for the rest of the process. Ronin builds each with a fresh `Builder`, so nothing carries.\n\nEvery field derived from the total is affected with it — `%t`, `%r`, `%p`, and the ETA weighting — so this is one accounting question, not four. It also shows after a regeneration that failed and reported itself, which is the shape that surfaced it.\n\nExit status agrees (0), so this is a progress-rendering defect. A conformance BuildCase needs `stale_manifest: true` and a generator edge, which the harness already supports; add it with the fix."
            }
        )
    }

    {
        id ronin-rust-2024-edition
        title "Compile the Ronin workspace with Rust 2024 semantics"
        kind @build
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-08-11T14:30:45.901769577Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
            }

            {
                at 2026-08-11T14:38:43.398932931Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Done. The root package now declares edition 2024 and the workspace uses dependency resolver 3; kati was already edition 2024. The compiler-guided migration renamed the private Node.gen field to Node.generator rather than carrying raw identifiers, added explicit empty RPIT captures where Rust 2024 would otherwise widen them, and applied the edition's rustfmt layout. Restored the MAKEFLAGS scheduler update as the valid Rust 2024 let-chain that prompted this correction, then collapsed the remaining Clippy-identified nested conditionals into let-chains. Audited the four tail-expression drop-order warnings emitted by cargo fix: they concern ownership-only temporaries in graph comparison, a consumed worklist Option, an owned evaluated byte value, and a spawn Result after its payload is moved; none retains a lock, descriptor, or other side effect across the changed boundary. Verification: cargo fmt --all -- --check; cargo check --workspace --all-targets; cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings; cargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast (690 passed, one deliberately ignored); the known cold manifest-reload flake was reproduced once, then passed 12/12 focused reruns and both warm suites; Ninja conformance passed all 425 upstream tests plus 10 differential, 86 build-outcome, 3 invocation-boundary, persistence, and log-content cases; Make conformance remained 301/387 normalized with every difference classified; direct/manifest Make graph equivalence compared 276 graphs with zero disagreements."
            }

